## Part 3: State Diagrams for Key Workflows

### **Workflow 1: Tenant Lifecycle**

```
┌─────────────┐
│   NEW PG    │
│  (No data)  │
└──────┬──────┘
       │
       ▼ Admin creates tenant record
┌─────────────────────┐
│ TENANT_CREATED      │
│ (Room assigned)     │
│ Status: ACTIVE      │
└──────┬──────────────┘
       │
       ├─ Move-in date today? → Check-in flow (v2)
       │
       ├─ Rent due in 30 days → Payment tracking
       │
       ├─ Admin marks vacant?
       │  └──▶ Status: VACATED
       │       └──▶ Room reverts to AVAILABLE
       │
       └─ Tenant reports issue?
          └──▶ Complaint created (v2)

KEY STATE TRANSITIONS:
ACTIVE → NOTICE_PERIOD (admin marks) → VACATED
  └─ Only admin can change status
  └─ Immutable history kept
```

